-- title:
--   Transported Igusa nodes over supersingular places, q = 2
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q = 2$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$; let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, and write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`. Let $W$ be a finite set whose members are exactly the supersingular places of `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,M'$ over $\kappa$ (rational, affine geometric, with $\mathrm{ev}(j_{\mathrm{geom}})$ in the supersingular $j$-set). Assume `modularFunctionFieldBar` $M' \le$ `fieldBar` $q\,M'$, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar` $M'$ to `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,M'$ whose residue is computed coefficientwise on Laurent series over $A$. Fix a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, and families $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ and $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{ss}}$ indexed by $W$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar` $q\,M'$, subject to: $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at the line $\infty = [1:0]$ is the Gauss ring of fractions of Laurent series over $A$ with reduced denominator nonzero; each $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is the pullback of the $\infty$-ring along some `levelAutBar` $q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ moving $\infty$ to the given line; injectivity of $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{Ig}}$; permutation of the family by all `levelAutBar` $\zeta'\,\gamma$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{ss}}_s \cap \overline{\mathbb{Q}} = A$; $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$-integrality and congruence, modulo the maximal ideal, of those $R_0$-integral functions regular wherever $j$ is and with residue integral at $s$; invariance of each $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ under all these level automorphisms; and existence in $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ of an element $t$ with $t - a$ a unit for all $a \in A$. Let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ to `fieldBar` $q\,M'$ with values in `xHFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,(q^2M')\,($`levelH` $q\,M')$ whose integers are $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\infty$, and assume $R_0$-integrality of $f$ is equivalent to $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\infty$-integrality of its image. Let $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ be a set of places of `xHFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,(q^2M')\,($`levelH` $q\,M')$ with $|N^{\mathrm{Ig}}| = |W|$, for which some ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,M'$ intertwines the residues of $R_0$ and $R$ and cuts out $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ as the places lying, via $j$, over the members of $W$. Finally let $g$ assign to each line an $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphism of `fieldBar` $q\,M'$ lying in the subgroup generated by all `levelAutBar` $\zeta'\,\gamma$ ($\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$) and equal to `levelAutBar` $q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ carrying $\infty$ to that line. The conclusion asserts a family $xs$ of places of `xHFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,(q^2M')\,($`levelH` $q\,M')$, indexed by lines and by $W$, all lying in $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$, such that for every line there is a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,M'$ to that field with: $g$ of the image of any $R_0$-integral $f$ is $R$-integral with $R$-residue $j(R_0\text{-residue of } f)$; for each $s \in W$ and each $g'$, integrality of $g'$ at $s$ is equivalent to integrality of $j(g')$ at $xs$ of the line and $s$; $j$ is $\kappa$-linear, commuting with the structure maps from $\kappa$; and $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ consists exactly of the places lying over members of $W$ via this $j$.
--
--   This provides, for each point of $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$, the set of Igusa nodes sitting over the supersingular places of the level-$M'$ curve, obtained by transporting the data at the $\infty$-chart along a level automorphism, together with the $\kappa$-linearity of the transported reduction map and the full characterisation of the nodes. It is the $q = 2$ form, under a rigidifying auxiliary prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the node-matching step used in assembling the semistable covering of the full-level modular curve; it is cited in the construction of that covering together with its equivalence clauses.
